# The Render Foundation

The v0.2 render foundation is the layer that lets {{ siteName }} render a page without an HTTP server. It preserves typed generated inputs instead of falling back to a `map[string]any`.

## Why it matters

Before the foundation, rendering was tied to `net/http`. That made SSG and Wails awkward. The foundation extracts a target-neutral typed App and renderer, so the same page can be served, pre-rendered, or embedded.

- Typed inputs stay the primary contract
- Non-HTTP rendering is explicit, not a nil-request hack
- Future targets build on one shared render path

## What stays the same

The server section still owns the data. The body still renders the same way. Only the plumbing around it changed.

